<title>UK: TABLE-Lloyds TSB H1 pretax up 33 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Lloyds TSB H1 pretax up 33 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		20.4	    vs 13.7</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.3	     vs 4.2</p>
<p> Pretax		     1,504	   vs 1,130</p>
<p> Total income	     3,586	   vs 3,347</p>
<p> Bad debt provision     229	     vs 214</p>
<p> Trading surplus	  1,733	   vs 1,416</p>
<p> Total assets	     156,329	 vs 152,566</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits between 1.47 billion  and 1.555 billion stg. Full name of the British bank is Lloyds TSB  Group Plc. The pretax figure is before a write-down of finance leases  of 58 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
